<title>USA: Code-Alarm says loses patent case.</title>
<headline>Code-Alarm says loses patent case.</headline>
<dateline>MADISON HEIGHTS, Mich. 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Code-Alarm Inc said Wednesday that a U.S. district court judge has ruled against the company in a patent infringement case.</p>
<p>Code-Alarm said the judge issued a permanent injunction related to two shock sensors that it no longer manufactures or sells.</p>
<p>It said a trial for damages in the matter is scheduled to begin later this month.</p>
<p>The company did not provide details about the case and a company official was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Code-Alarm makes and sells electronic vehicle security devices.</p>
</text>
